[00:11.78]Jehovah is our refuge,
[00:16.78]Our God in whom we trust.
[00:22.60]His shadow is our shelter;
[00:28.08]Remain in it we must.
[00:33.84]His faithful ones he will defend,
[00:39.46]On this we know we can depend.
[00:44.98]Jehovah is a stronghold,
[00:50.70]Ever faithful, loyal, and just.
[01:04.92]Though thousands will have fallen
[01:09.38]And many at our side,
[01:15.20]The righteous and the meek ones
[01:21.72]Will never be denied.
[01:27.34]So in our hearts we need not fear;
[01:32.91]Calamity will not come near.
[01:38.50]From danger he will shield us,
[01:44.03]For beneath God’s wings we’ll reside.
[02:23.92]He’ll keep us and protect us
[02:29.10]From snares along our way,
[02:34.34]From terrors in the nighttime,
[02:40.88]And arrows by the day.
[02:46.06]Yes, there will be no cause for dread,
[02:52.06]No place where we will fear to tread.
[02:58.12]Jehovah is our refuge,
[03:03.48]Ever guarding us on our way.
